## Answers to the five business questions

1. **Who churns?** Month-to-month customers churn {{ s.m2m.churn_rate | pct }} ({{ a.constants.ci_level_pct }}% CI {{ s.m2m.ci_low | pct }} to {{ s.m2m.ci_high | pct }}), against
   {{ s.one_year.churn_rate | pct }} on one-year and {{ s.two_year.churn_rate | pct }} on two-year contracts. First-year customers churn {{ s.tenure_0_12.churn_rate | pct }};
   fiber-optic {{ s.fiber.churn_rate | pct }}; electronic-check payers {{ s.echeck.churn_rate | pct }}; customers without tech support {{ s.no_tech_support.churn_rate | pct }}.
   ![Churn by segment](reports/figures/01_churn_by_segment.png)
2. **What does it cost?** {{ k.mrr_lost | usd }} a month ({{ k.annual_revenue_lost | usd }} a year). Month-to-month contracts are {{ s.m2m_share_of_customers | pct(0) }} of customers but
   {{ s.m2m_share_of_mrr_lost | pct(0) }} of the loss. One segment, new month-to-month fiber customers ({{ a.revenue_at_risk.hot_customers | num }} people,
   {{ a.revenue_at_risk.hot_share_of_customers | pct(0) }} of the base), churns {{ a.revenue_at_risk.hot_churn_rate | pct(0) }} and carries {{ a.revenue_at_risk.hot_share_of_mrr_lost | pct(0) }} of lost revenue.
   ![Revenue at risk](reports/figures/02_revenue_at_risk.png)
3. **Strongest drivers.** Chi-square tests with Cramer's V (categories) and Mann-Whitney with rank-biserial r (numbers), Bonferroni-corrected:
   {% for d in a.drivers.top[:4] %}{{ d.label | lower }} ({{ d.effect | sig }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
   {{ a.drivers.n_significant }} of {{ a.drivers.n_tested }} features are significant; gender is not (V = {{ a.drivers.gender_v | sig(3) }}, p = {{ a.drivers.gender_p | sig }}).
   Kaplan-Meier: only {{ a.survival.m2m_s72 | pct(0) }} of month-to-month customers would still be active at {{ a.constants.survival_checkpoints[2] }} months, against
   {{ a.survival.two_year_s72 | pct(0) }} on two-year contracts (log-rank p < {{ a.constants.p_floor }}).
   ![Kaplan-Meier](reports/figures/04_kaplan_meier_contract.png)
4. **Risk scoring and its value.** Logistic regression, random forest and gradient boosting were compared with {{ m.protocol.cv_folds }}-fold stratified cross-validation.
   **The tree models did not beat the logistic-regression baseline** (CV ROC-AUC {% for r in mo.table %}{% if r.model != "Logistic regression (class-weighted)" %}{{ r.model | lower }} {{ r.cv_roc_auc | sig(3) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}),
   so the simpler, explainable model is used. The riskiest 10% of test customers churn at {{ m.lift.top_decile_lift | sig(1) }}x the average and the riskiest three deciles contain {{ m.lift.top3_capture | pct(0) }} of churners.
   ![Lift and gains](reports/figures/12_lift_gains.png)
5. **Campaign break-even and best target group.** The offer costs {{ ca.contact_cost | money }} to deliver plus {{ ca.offer_discount_pct }}% of the bill for {{ ca.offer_months }} months.
   Targeting threshold chosen to maximise net value on training folds: {{ th.chosen | sig }}; on the untouched test set it reaches recall {{ th.test_recall | pct(0) }} at precision {{ th.test_precision | pct(0) }}.

   | Target group | Customers | Churn rate | Net value | ROI | Break-even save rate |
   |---|---|---|---|---|---|
   | **Model: probability >= {{ th.chosen | sig }}** | {{ g.customers | num }} | {{ g.churn_rate | pct }} | **{{ g.net_value | usd }}** | {{ g.roi | pct(0) }} | {{ g.breakeven_save_rate | pct }} |
   | Rule: month-to-month + fiber + first year | {{ c.groups.rule_m2m_fiber_first_year.customers | num }} | {{ c.groups.rule_m2m_fiber_first_year.churn_rate | pct }} | {{ c.groups.rule_m2m_fiber_first_year.net_value | usd }} | {{ c.groups.rule_m2m_fiber_first_year.roi | pct(0) }} | {{ c.groups.rule_m2m_fiber_first_year.breakeven_save_rate | pct }} |
   | All month-to-month | {{ c.groups.all_month_to_month.customers | num }} | {{ c.groups.all_month_to_month.churn_rate | pct }} | {{ c.groups.all_month_to_month.net_value | usd }} | {{ c.groups.all_month_to_month.roi | pct(0) }} | {{ c.groups.all_month_to_month.breakeven_save_rate | pct }} |
